  "summary": "Full assessment of all 167 classical-Japanese/Vietnamese units — Bashō’s travel prose and every haiku and waka — and both titles. The departure from Fukagawa, Nikkō, Shirakawa, Matsushima, Hiraizumi, Ryūshakuji, the Mogami, Dewa Sanzan, Kisakata, the Echigo coast, Kanazawa, Yamanaka and Ōgaki are complete, with the Chinese and Japanese allusions and the place-name puns kept. The separate-context pass scored 8.725 with no major findings and twenty minor ones, chiefly haiku padding and a few prose misparses; those were revised. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "おくのほそ道",
    "target_title": "Lối lên miền Oku",
    "rationale": "Lối lên miền Oku is the established Vietnamese title (Vĩnh Sính’s translation); lên fits a journey north, and the body names the Oku no hosomichi itself."
  }
